From 43a2196f3681a7315381ee3e8143e87bdb26e9ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 12:17:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] chore(scripts): add commit-beads-hooks.sh + make
 targets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Companion to update-beads-hooks.sh. After a bd binary upgrade,
`make update-hooks` rewrites every repo's .beads/hooks/* shims (bumping the
BEGIN/END BEADS INTEGRATION markers), leaving 100+ dirty working trees. This
sweeps them: one path-scoped commit per repo touching ONLY .beads/hooks/.

  make commit-hooks          - commit, no push
  make commit-hooks-push     - commit, then git push each repo
  make commit-hooks-dry-run  - show what would be committed

Path-scoped partial commit (no `git add`) so unrelated staged changes stay
staged and untracked/gitignored shims are never swept in. Skips worktrees,
non-git dirs, generated agent-home trees (~/.claude-*, ~/.codex-*, ~/.pi-*,
~/.config/goose/* — read-only persona skill copies wiped on rebuild), and
repos with no tracked .beads/hooks/ changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
